\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Enlarged regions showing a recovery case and a reference-score failure case. All columns show identical image pixels within each row. Blue boxes are existing reference annotations; green boxes are matched predictions; dashed red boxes are missed references; orange boxes are unmatched predictions. Counts use local class-aware, one-to-one matching at IoU 0.50 and confidence 0.25; boxes enter a region by their center. Examples were selected after inspecting saved outputs to maximize and minimize the local WBF-4 gain over the single model. They illustrate differences, not their average frequency. Existing annotation omissions can make a real component appear as an unmatched prediction.\relax }}{3}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:qualitative}{{2}{3}{Enlarged regions showing a recovery case and a reference-score failure case. All columns show identical image pixels within each row. Blue boxes are existing reference annotations; green boxes are matched predictions; dashed red boxes are missed references; orange boxes are unmatched predictions. Counts use local class-aware, one-to-one matching at IoU 0.50 and confidence 0.25; boxes enter a region by their center. Examples were selected after inspecting saved outputs to maximize and minimize the local WBF-4 gain over the single model. They illustrate differences, not their average frequency. Existing annotation omissions can make a real component appear as an unmatched prediction.\relax }{figure.caption.11}{}}
